{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-65435","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95716","text":"Graphonomous FAQ"}]},{"id":"blk-65436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95717","text":"This page answers the most common questions about Graphonomous, its MCP interface, and operating model."}]},{"id":"blk-65437","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95718","text":"What is Graphonomous?"}]},{"id":"blk-65438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95719","text":"Graphonomous is a continual-learning memory engine for AI agents. It stores knowledge as a graph, supports confidence-updating feedback loops, and exposes all capabilities through MCP tools/resources."}]},{"id":"blk-65439","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95720","text":"Does Graphonomous retrain model weights?"}]},{"id":"blk-65440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95721","text":"No. Graphonomous does "},{"id":"spn-95722","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-95723","text":" retrain model weights. Learning happens in the memory graph by storing knowledge and updating confidence based on outcomes."}]},{"id":"blk-65441","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-95724","text":"What problem does it solve?"}]},{"id":"blk-65442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95725","text":"It gives agents durable, evolving memory and better decision quality over time by combining:"}]},{"id":"blk-65443","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95726","text":"semantic retrieval"}]}],"id":"blk-65444","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95727","text":"graph neighborhood expansion"}]}],"id":"blk-65446","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95728","text":"causal outcome feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-65448","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-95729","text":"goal tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-65450","kind"